auth {
  mode: apikey
}

auth:apikey {
  key: X-Auth-Token
  value: {{token}}
  placement: header
}

docs {
  # Catalyst Center SWIM (2.3.7.x)

  Classic SWIM flow over the Intent API, with a port maintenance window around the reload:
  token > find device and image > (import) > (golden) > snapshot + shut ports > distribute > activate >
  poll task > verify > re-enable ports > check.

  Every request except "Get token" inherits the X-Auth-Token header from this collection.
  Run "01 Auth / Get token" first; it stores `token` as a runtime variable (valid about 60 min).

  Runtime variables set by scripts: `token`, `deviceUuid`, `deviceCurrentVersion`, `imageUuid`,
  `imageVersion`, `deviceFamilyId`, `taskId`.

  Port runtime variables: `portQueue`, `currentPortId`, `currentPortName`, `fileId`.
  The pre-change port state is kept in the environment variable `portSnapshot`.

  Safety switches (environment):
  - `allowPortChanges: true` is needed for the shut / no shut requests.
  - `allowActivation: true` is needed for activation, which reloads the device.
}
